infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Anemic vs rich domain model
  desc Where behavior lives decides who can break the invariants
  compares
    - label Anemic domain model
      children
        - label Data bags, logic in services
          desc Fields, getters, setters — no behavior on the object
        - label Any caller mutates via setters
          desc A direct setStatus() bypasses every service check
        - label Invariants scattered across methods
          desc A rule lives wherever a developer happened to write it
        - label Right for genuinely simple CRUD
          desc Reference data, two-state entities, throwaway scripts
    - label Rich domain model
      children
        - label Behavior co-located with data
          desc The object owns its state and every transition
        - label State changes via intent methods
          desc order.confirm() and cancel(), not public setters
        - label Invariants enforced at each boundary
          desc Every transition checks its preconditions first
        - label Earns its cost on real complexity
          desc Many callers, lifecycle rules that grow over time
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
